Extension: did not get suggestions for Meta::RunContext::* enum values

need to red/green test and ensure we handle all this fine regardless of how deep it is

## DIAGNOSIS (coordinator, 2026-08-31) — root-caused, not yet fixed

Confirmed by reading the source. The data is present and correct: the typedb
has `{"ns": "Meta", "id": 74, "name": "RunContext", ...}` with a full `values`
map (`Main`, `BeforeScripts`, `MainLoop`, ...). Nothing is missing from the
dump. The completion path never asks for it.

**This is not specific to `Meta::RunContext`. NO enum has ever offered its
values after `::`.** The reporter hit the general case.

### Two stacked defects — fixing either alone still yields nothing

`complete` (`src/server/completion.rs:48`) routes a `::` prefix to
`complete_namespace_members` (`:89`), which is a one-line delegation to
`TypeIndex::source_scope_members` (`src/typedb/index.rs:1030`).

**Defect 1 — the gate rejects the path before any lookup.**
`source_scope_members` opens with `if !self.scope_exists(scope) { return
Vec::new(); }`, and `scope_exists` is just `self.scopes.contains(path)`.
`build_scope_index` (`src/typedb/index.rs:686`) inserts, for a Core enum, only
**its namespace** — `Meta` — never the enum itself. So
`scope_exists("Meta::RunContext")` is **false** and the function returns empty
before doing anything.

**Defect 2 — the enumeration has no enum-value branch anyway.**
`source_scope_members` walks exactly three collections: `source_names` (types
and enum *names*), `functions`, and `scopes` (nested namespaces). Enum
**values** live in `EnumInfo::values` and are read by nothing on this path.

So the fix must address both. A change that only makes the enum a scope returns
an empty list; a change that only adds the value branch never reaches it.

### The doc already claims this works

`src/server/completion.rs:6` reads:

    //! 2. `::` at cursor → namespace member / enum value / nested type

"enum value" has been in that list the whole time and was never implemented.
Worth noting in the fix: this is a case where the module doc described intent
and was read as description.

### Why it was never caught

Enum values ARE offered — but only by the **namespace-shortcut** path
(`shortcut_match_enums`, `completion.rs:453-500`), which is a different
feature: it offers `UI::Cond::Always` in *identifier* position when the user
has configured shortcut namespaces. Every enum-value completion test in the
tree (`:1384`, `:1406`, `:1429`) exercises that path. **The `::` path has no
enum-value coverage at all**, which is exactly why a whole missing branch sat
behind a doc line claiming it existed.

## DO NOT FIX IT AT `scope_exists`

Tempting and wrong. `scope_exists` is the typechecker's notion of a valid
namespace path; widening it to include enums would make the CHECKER start
accepting paths *through* an enum (`Meta::RunContext::Main::Whatever`) and
would change diagnostics far from completion. B067 already moved this
predicate once and B079 exists because two nearly-identical scope/enum
predicates were being picked wrongly at call sites — do not add a third
meaning to this one.

**Fix in the completion path instead**: when the `::` qualifier resolves to an
enum, offer its values; otherwise fall through to `source_scope_members` as
today. Completion asking a different question from the typechecker is correct
here — "what can follow `::` in the editor" genuinely is a broader set than
"what is a namespace".

## Test plan (TDD, red first) — generalise per CLAUDE.md

The reporter's note "regardless of how deep it is" is the real requirement.
Cover each enum SHAPE, since they reach the index by different routes in
`build_scope_index`:

- **Core enum in a namespace** — `Meta::RunContext::` (the report), `UI::Cond::`
- **Core enum at global scope** — `SomeEnum::`
- **Nadeo enum under a class scope** — the `Module::Scope::Name` form whose
  module segment is dropped; e.g. `CGameMenu::EMenuOrder::`
- **Deeply nested** — a class-scope enum two or more segments down
- **Workspace-declared enum**, plain and inside a `namespace`
- **A workspace enum shadowing an engine one** — must offer the workspace values
- Kind should be `ENUM_MEMBER`, not `FUNCTION` (`complete_namespace_members`
  currently hardcodes `CompletionItemKind::FUNCTION` for everything it emits —
  check whether that is wrong for the existing cases too, and say so rather
  than silently changing it).

**Required silences, in the same fixture as the successes** — otherwise "offer
everything after `::`" passes:

- a genuine namespace (`Meta::`) still offers its members and NOT enum values
  from enums inside it
- an anonymous/synthetic member-enum key must not leak (B016 already guards
  this on the shortcut path; the `::` path needs its own guard)
- an unknown qualifier (`ZZZNoSuch::`) still offers nothing

Game-probing is NOT required — this is editor UX, not engine semantics. The
engine question ("is `Meta::RunContext::Main` valid?") is already settled by
the typedb.